# Alarm settings: one KEY=VALUE per line (the team's tool protocol V4.12, rule H4; same format as tools/ctx_grade). No quotes, no
# $variables, no ~, no commands: _tools/settings_v1.py reads this file as text and refuses an unknown key. Copy it to
# settings/SETTINGS_<MACHINE>.env, put this machine's paths in, and name that file in every command:
#   python3 -B _tools/settings_v1.py check settings/SETTINGS_<MACHINE>.env
# Every value is an absolute path outside the Alarm folder (only data lives outside), or empty when this machine does not have it.
#
# PYTHON: the interpreter for real runs: Python 3.10 or 3.11 with the packages in settings/PYTHON_PACKAGES.txt.
PYTHON=/path/to/python3
# LAB_DAYS: the lab days, LAB1's lab3 store (bars, prints, liquidations, OI per coin and day). Read only.
LAB_DAYS=/path/to/lab_days
# RESEARCH_STORE: QUANT's shared research store. alarm_profile edition 1 writes the A02 profiles there; editions 2 and later refuse it.
RESEARCH_STORE=/path/to/research_days
# HL_FILLS: Hyperliquid fills (npz per day), read by alarm_profile's hyperliquid block (A02 subjects only). Empty = that block NOT_KNOWN.
HL_FILLS=/path/to/hl_fills_npz
# SCRATCH: the big scratch disk: build out roots and outcome tables before they are extracted.
SCRATCH=/path/to/scratch
# RESEARCH_ROOT: the research data, in the team's layout: ALARM_DESIGN (definitions, cards, registry, runs and their PERFIRE files) and
# tools/<tool>/inputs, receipts, results. Runs read their inputs and write their outputs under it, never inside Alarm.
RESEARCH_ROOT=/path/to/research
# BOARD: the team board folder (hb, one <SEAT>.txt per seat): the kit's board_line and audit write and read it. Empty = no board here.
BOARD=/path/to/hb
# RUNNER_QUEUES: the job runner (Q_V1..Q_V21, each with IN and RUN). Empty = jobs cannot be queued on this machine.
RUNNER_QUEUES=
# RUNNER_ALLOC: the job runner's job number allocator (job_alloc.py; it keeps its claims beside the runner, so it is run where it is,
# never copied into Alarm). Empty = jobs cannot be queued on this machine.
RUNNER_ALLOC=
# RUNNER_RELEASE: the Alarm release folder the job runner runs jobs from, as a path on the runner's machine (the queue fills a job's
# @@ALARM@@ with it). Empty = the Alarm folder the queue itself runs from (queueing on the runner's machine, from the install). Set it
# on a machine that queues for another one, e.g. a VM that sees the runner's folders under other paths.
RUNNER_RELEASE=
# FEED_GATE: the live feed's batch gate file (first line RUN or PAUSE): detect waits while it reads PAUSE, so a batch job never runs
# during the feed's backfill. Empty = no feed on this machine, no gate (detect runs at once).
FEED_GATE=
# FORBID: the code folder no run may read (the team's dev tree), so every run proves its isolation. Empty = isolation not checked.
FORBID=
